{
	"name": "Spellcasting",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-etched-steel-blade.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 1st level, you begin to learn the simple, yet potent, brand of spellcasting for which warcasters are known.</p><h2>Cantrips</h2><p>You know four cantrips of your choice from the warcaster spell list. You learn additional warcaster cantrips of your choice at higher levels, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Warcaster table.</p><p>Additionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the warcaster cantrips you know and replace it with another warcaster cantrip.</p><p></p><h2>Spellcasting Ability</h2><p>Your spellcasting ability score is determined by your initiation but will be either your Intelligence or Charisma. In either case, you’ll use the modifier for this ability in the following calculations to determine your spell save DC and your spell attack modifier:</p><p><strong>Spell save DC</strong> = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Spellcasting modifier</p><p><strong>Spell attack modifier</strong> = your proficiency bonus + your Spellcasting modifier</p><p></p><h2>Spellcasting Focus</h2><p>Warcasters may use any arcane focus, or spell component pouch, to cast their spells. However, they can also use any melee or ranged weapon as an arcane focus for the purposes of spellcasting.</p>",
